# A bad-bot list that does what the generated one should: it refuses the bots and the HTTP
# libraries it names, and nothing a site wants. As the generated one is, it is a fragment
# for a frontend, and the test runs it first, so that the checks on the bad-bot list are
# shown to pass on a list that is right.
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i sqlmap
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i AhrefsBot
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i SemrushBot
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i MJ12bot
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i curl
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i python-requests
acl bad_bot hdr_sub(User-Agent) -i Go-http-client
http-request deny if bad_bot
